# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# js/ and css/ change on almost every deploy. Cloudflare's default
# (max-age=14400) let the edge and the browser keep serving the old file
# for hours after a deploy, which is why these used to carry a ?v=NN
# query — a hand-bumped counter that was easy to forget and, worse, could
# pin a stale copy to the new query string if anything fetched it during
# the deploy. no-cache keeps the file cached but forces a revalidation on
# every request, so a deploy is picked up on the next page load and the
# usual response is a cheap 304.
/js/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/css/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
